node_modules/
tests/shots/

# Credentials and machine-local state. Nothing of this kind exists in the project
# today and none of it is tracked; these patterns are here so that going public
# cannot be the moment one gets committed by accident. `.npmrc` matters most: it
# is where an npm auth token lands, and it sits at the repository root.
.env
.env.*
.npmrc
.netrc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
.DS_Store
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/

# Raw research-agent output. Kept local on purpose: the curated documents in
# docs/knowledge-base/ carry the findings, and they cite these filenames as
# provenance labels rather than as links.
docs/knowledge-base/raw/

# Process and retrospective documents. These describe how the project was built
# rather than how to use it, so they are kept local. The security AUDIT lives
# here too; the repo carries SECURITY.md, which is a disclosure policy instead.
docs/assets-provenance.md
docs/design-review.md
docs/lessons-learned.md
docs/security.md

# AI assistant config, memory and working state. Kept local on purpose: it is
# machine-specific, changes constantly, and is not part of the project.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/
.claude-flow/
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.windsurfrules
.aider*
.roo/
.mcp.json
.continue/
.github/copilot-instructions.md
